a. fast, safe, and empathetic;
b. guarantee of confidentiality;
c. easily accessible; andd. not charged.

Article 12

1. The community has obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence as referred to in Article 10 letter b which is implemented in the form of community participation.
2. Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) include:a. forming family partners at the kelurahan level;
b. forming women and children protection units within community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of women's and children's rights;
d. providing first aid to victims; ande. reporting to the competent authority if violence against victims occurs in their environment.

CHAPTER VIII

